IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tco-dates`

-- Coroners Act 1995 (Tas) -- the rules that a family member of a person who has died, and anyone else with a claim
-- touching the death (or a fire or explosion), meets: who is the senior next of kin (s 3A), what is a reportable death
-- (s 3) and the duty to report it (s 19), when an inquest must or may be held (ss 21, 23, 24, 24A, 26A), adjournment for
-- criminal charges (s 25), the requests and the Supreme Court applications with their 14-day and 48-hour time limits
-- (ss 26, 26A, 27, 37, 38, 39, 42, 44), the bars on autopsy, exhumation and the disposal certificate (ss 32, 38(2),
-- 39(2), (3)), the rights of an interested person at an inquest (s 52), what may be used in evidence (ss 29(2), 46(2),
-- 54, 64), reopening and voiding findings (ss 58, 58A), copies of coronial records (s 58C), property held by the coroner
-- (ss 59A(4), 60-63) and the penalties (ss 19, 20, 34, 42, 49, 53, 57, 58C, 65, 66).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in tco-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule.
-- Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("means", "must not", "is not",
-- "only ... if", an "if", "where" or "unless" condition that fails, a period the Act fixes that has passed); or NOTHING
-- where the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. The coroner's, the Chief
-- Magistrate's and the Supreme Court's judgments ("considers", "is satisfied", "believes", "reason to the contrary",
-- "sufficient interest", "not available") are inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess at them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of Tasmania, CC BY
-- 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Coroners Act 1995`

§§ `s 3A -- the senior next of kin`

-- s 3A: "the senior next of kin of a deceased person is -- (a) if a person was, immediately before the death ..., the
-- only spouse ..., that spouse; or (b) if the deceased person ... is survived by more than one person who would qualify
-- as the deceased person's spouse, the last person to so qualify; or (c) if ... the spouse referred to in paragraph (b)
-- is not available, another spouse ... if that spouse has the approval of the spouse referred to in paragraph (b); or
-- (d) if the person referred to in paragraph (a), (b) or (c) is not available, a child ... if the child has attained the
-- age of 18 years; or (e) if [none above] is available, the person with whom the deceased person had a caring
-- relationship ... the subject of a deed of relationship registered under Part 2 of the Relationships Act 2003; or (f)
-- ... a parent ...; or (g) ... a sibling ... if the sibling has attained the age of 18 years; or (h) ... an executor
-- named in the will ... or a person who, immediately before the death, was a personal representative ...; or (i) if the
-- deceased person is an Aboriginal person, a person who, according to the customs and tradition of the community or
-- group to which the person belongs, is an appropriate person." s 3: "spouse includes the other party to a significant
-- relationship, within the meaning of the Relationships Act 2003". "Not available" is not defined: asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Relationship to the deceased` IS ONE OF
    `the spouse or significant-relationship partner`
    `a child`
    `the partner in a registered caring relationship`
    `a parent`
    `a sibling`
    `an executor or personal representative`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `Senior next of kin answer` IS ONE OF
    `you are the senior next of kin`
    `you are one of several people equally placed to be the senior next of kin`
    `you may be the senior next of kin as the appropriate person by Aboriginal custom`
    `you are not the senior next of kin: someone ranked above you is available`
    `you are not the senior next of kin on these facts`

-- The rank under s 3A(a)-(h) of a relationship (1 highest); 0 for none.
GIVEN r IS A `Relationship to the deceased`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 3A rank of` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `the spouse or significant-relationship partner` THEN 1
    WHEN `a child` THEN 2
    WHEN `the partner in a registered caring relationship` THEN 3
    WHEN `a parent` THEN 4
    WHEN `a sibling` THEN 5
    WHEN `an executor or personal representative` THEN 6
    WHEN `none of these` THEN 0

GIVEN `my relationship` IS A `Relationship to the deceased`
      `I am 18 or over` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was the only spouse immediately before the death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased left more than one spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was the last to qualify as a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last spouse is available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last spouse approves me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a spouse is available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult child is available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registered caring partner is available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a parent is available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult sibling is available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another person of my kind is available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased was an Aboriginal person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am the appropriate person by custom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Senior next of kin answer`
`s 3A -- am I the senior next of kin` `my relationship` `I am 18 or over` `I was the only spouse immediately before the death` `the deceased left more than one spouse` `I was the last to qualify as a spouse` `the last spouse is available` `the last spouse approves me` `a spouse is available` `an adult child is available` `the registered caring partner is available` `a parent is available` `an adult sibling is available` `another person of my kind is available` `the deceased was an Aboriginal person` `I am the appropriate person by custom` MEANS
    IF `my ranked answer` EQUALS `you are the senior next of kin`
       OR `my ranked answer` EQUALS `you are one of several people equally placed to be the senior next of kin`
    THEN `my ranked answer`
    ELSE IF `the deceased was an Aboriginal person` AND `I am the appropriate person by custom`
         THEN `you may be the senior next of kin as the appropriate person by Aboriginal custom`
         ELSE `my ranked answer`
    WHERE
        `the rank` MEANS `the s 3A rank of` `my relationship`
        `someone above is available` MEANS
               (`the rank` GREATER THAN 1 AND `a spouse is available`)
            OR (`the rank` GREATER THAN 2 AND `an adult child is available`)
            OR (`the rank` GREATER THAN 3 AND `the registered caring partner is available`)
            OR (`the rank` GREATER THAN 4 AND `a parent is available`)
            OR (`the rank` GREATER THAN 5 AND `an adult sibling is available`)
        `the spouse answer` MEANS
            IF `the deceased left more than one spouse`
            THEN IF `I was the last to qualify as a spouse`
                 THEN `you are the senior next of kin`
                 ELSE IF (NOT `the last spouse is available`) AND `the last spouse approves me`
                      THEN IF `another person of my kind is available`
                           THEN `you are one of several people equally placed to be the senior next of kin`
                           ELSE `you are the senior next of kin`
                      ELSE `you are not the senior next of kin on these facts`
            ELSE IF `I was the only spouse immediately before the death`
                 THEN `you are the senior next of kin`
                 ELSE `you are not the senior next of kin on these facts`
        `the lower answer` MEANS
            IF (`my relationship` EQUALS `a child` OR `my relationship` EQUALS `a sibling`) AND (NOT `I am 18 or over`)
            THEN `you are not the senior next of kin on these facts`
            ELSE IF `someone above is available`
                 THEN `you are not the senior next of kin: someone ranked above you is available`
                 ELSE IF `another person of my kind is available` AND (NOT (`my relationship` EQUALS `the partner in a registered caring relationship`))
                      THEN `you are one of several people equally placed to be the senior next of kin`
                      ELSE `you are the senior next of kin`
        `my ranked answer` MEANS
            CONSIDER `my relationship`
            WHEN `none of these` THEN `you are not the senior next of kin on these facts`
            WHEN `the spouse or significant-relationship partner` THEN `the spouse answer`
            OTHERWISE `the lower answer`

-- s 3B(1): "If a person is aggrieved by a decision made under this Act specifying who is the senior next of kin ..., the
-- person may appeal the decision to the Supreme Court." An "if" condition: JUST FALSE when it fails.
GIVEN `a decision specifying the senior next of kin has been made` IS A BOOLEAN, `I am aggrieved by it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3B -- I may appeal who is the senior next of kin` `a decision specifying the senior next of kin has been made` `I am aggrieved by it` MEANS
    IF `a decision specifying the senior next of kin has been made` AND `I am aggrieved by it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 3 -- reportable death`

-- s 3: "reportable death means -- (a) a death where -- (i) the body ... is in Tasmania; or (ii) the death occurred in
-- Tasmania; or (iii) the cause of the death occurred in Tasmania; or (iiia) the death occurred while the person was
-- travelling from or to Tasmania -- being a death -- (iv) that appears to have been unexpected, unnatural or violent or
-- to have resulted directly or indirectly from an accident or injury; or (v) that occurs during a medical procedure, or
-- after [one] where the death may be causally related to that procedure, and a medical practitioner would not ... have
-- reasonably expected the death; or ... (vii) the cause of which is unknown; or (viii) of a child under the age of one
-- year which was sudden and unexpected; or (ix) of a person who immediately before death was a person held in care or
-- a person held in custody; or (x) of a person whose identity is unknown; or (xi) that occurs at, or as a result of an
-- accident or injury that occurs at, the deceased person's place of work, and does not appear to be due to natural
-- causes; or (b) the death of a person who ordinarily resided in Tasmania ... that occurred at a place outside Tasmania
-- where the cause of death is not certified by a person who, under a law in force in the place, is a medical
-- practitioner; or (c) the death of a person that occurred whilst that person was escaping or attempting to escape from
-- [custody]; or (d) the death of a person that occurred whilst a police officer, correctional officer, mental health
-- officer or a prescribed person ... was attempting to detain that person". "death includes suspected death".
-- A "means" definition: JUST FALSE when no limb holds.
DECLARE `Kind of death` IS ONE OF
    `unexpected, unnatural or violent, or from an accident or injury`
    `during or after a medical procedure, and not reasonably expected`
    `the cause is unknown`
    `sudden and unexpected death of a child under one`
    `a person held in care or in custody immediately before death`
    `a person whose identity is unknown`
    `at work, or from an accident or injury at work, and not apparently from natural causes`
    `while escaping or attempting to escape from custody`
    `while being detained by a police, correctional or mental health officer or prescribed person`
    `an expected death from natural causes, none of the above`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of death`
      `the body is in Tasmania` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the death occurred in Tasmania` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cause of death occurred in Tasmania` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was travelling to or from Tasmania` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person ordinarily resided in Tasmania and died outside it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cause was certified by a medical practitioner where they died` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3 -- it is a reportable death` `the kind` `the body is in Tasmania` `the death occurred in Tasmania` `the cause of death occurred in Tasmania` `the person was travelling to or from Tasmania` `the person ordinarily resided in Tasmania and died outside it` `the cause was certified by a medical practitioner where they died` MEANS
    IF `limb (c) or (d)` OR `limb (a)` OR `limb (b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `limb (c) or (d)` MEANS
               `the kind` EQUALS `while escaping or attempting to escape from custody`
            OR `the kind` EQUALS `while being detained by a police, correctional or mental health officer or prescribed person`
        `a Tasmanian connection` MEANS
               `the body is in Tasmania`
            OR `the death occurred in Tasmania`
            OR `the cause of death occurred in Tasmania`
            OR `the person was travelling to or from Tasmania`
        `limb (a)` MEANS
            `a Tasmanian connection` AND (NOT (`the kind` EQUALS `an expected death from natural causes, none of the above`))
        `limb (b)` MEANS
            `the person ordinarily resided in Tasmania and died outside it` AND (NOT `the cause was certified by a medical practitioner where they died`)

§§ `s 19 -- the duty to report a death`

-- s 19(1): "A person who has reasonable grounds to believe that a reportable death, other than a reportable death
-- referred to in subsection (4), has not been reported must report it as soon as possible to a coroner or a police
-- officer. Penalty: Fine not exceeding 10 penalty units." (3): "If more than one medical practitioner is present at or
-- after a death and one of them reports it ..., the other medical practitioners need not report the death but must give
-- to the coroner ... any information which may help the investigation." (4): a death in custody or care, while escaping,
-- or while being detained "must be reported as soon as possible to a coroner by the person in whose custody or care the
-- person was held or by the [officer] attempting to detain that person."
DECLARE `Reporting answer` IS ONE OF
    `you must report the death as soon as possible to a coroner or a police officer`
    `you must report the death as soon as possible to a coroner`
    `you need not report it, but must give the coroner any information that may help`
    `section 19 does not require you to report it`

GIVEN `I believe on reasonable grounds it is a reportable death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I believe on reasonable grounds it has not been reported` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a custody, care, escape or detention death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am the custodian or the officer concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a medical practitioner present and another present has reported it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Reporting answer`
`s 19 -- must I report the death` `I believe on reasonable grounds it is a reportable death` `I believe on reasonable grounds it has not been reported` `it is a custody, care, escape or detention death` `I am the custodian or the officer concerned` `I am a medical practitioner present and another present has reported it` MEANS
    IF `it is a custody, care, escape or detention death`
    THEN IF `I am the custodian or the officer concerned`
         THEN `you must report the death as soon as possible to a coroner`
         ELSE `section 19 does not require you to report it`
    ELSE IF `I am a medical practitioner present and another present has reported it`
         THEN `you need not report it, but must give the coroner any information that may help`
         ELSE IF `I believe on reasonable grounds it is a reportable death` AND `I believe on reasonable grounds it has not been reported`
              THEN `you must report the death as soon as possible to a coroner or a police officer`
              ELSE `section 19 does not require you to report it`

§§ `ss 27(1), 37(1), 42(1) -- asking the coroner`

-- s 27(1): "A person who a coroner considers has a sufficient interest in a death may request the coroner to hold an
-- inquest into the death." s 37(1): "If a coroner has jurisdiction to investigate a death, any person who the coroner
-- considers has a sufficient interest in the death may request the coroner to direct that an autopsy be performed".
-- s 42(1): "A person who the coroner considers has a sufficient interest in a fire or an explosion may request a coroner
-- to investigate the fire or explosion." Grants limited in their own wording: outside them, NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: a
-- grant limited in its own wording; the case falls outside the limit).
DECLARE `Request to the coroner` IS ONE OF
    `an inquest into a death`
    `an autopsy`
    `an investigation into a fire or explosion`

GIVEN `what I ask for` IS A `Request to the coroner`
      `the coroner considers I have a sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner has jurisdiction to investigate the death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 27, 37, 42 -- I may ask the coroner` `what I ask for` `the coroner considers I have a sufficient interest` `the coroner has jurisdiction to investigate the death` MEANS
    IF `the coroner considers I have a sufficient interest`
       AND (`the coroner has jurisdiction to investigate the death` OR (NOT (`what I ask for` EQUALS `an autopsy`)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 21, 23, 24, 24A, 26A -- the inquest into a death`

-- s 21(1): "A coroner has jurisdiction to investigate a death if it appears to the coroner that the death is or may be a
-- reportable death." (2): "Unless the Attorney-General directs otherwise, a coroner need not investigate a death if an
-- investigation or inquest is held in another State or in a Territory." s 23(4): if the approved Aboriginal
-- organisation reports that the remains are Aboriginal remains, "the jurisdiction of the coroner ... ceases and this Act
-- does not apply to the remains." s 24(1): "Subject to section 25, a coroner who has jurisdiction to investigate a death
-- must hold an inquest if the body is in Tasmania or it appears to the coroner that the death, or the cause of death,
-- occurred in Tasmania or that the deceased ordinarily resided in Tasmania at the time of death and -- (a) the coroner
-- suspects homicide; or (b) the deceased was immediately before death a person held in care or a person held in custody;
-- or (c) the identity of the deceased is not known; or (d) the deceased died whilst escaping or attempting to escape
-- from [custody]; or (e) the death occurred in the process of [an officer] attempting to detain a person; or (ea) the
-- deceased died at, or as a result of an accident or injury that occurred at, his or her place of work and the coroner
-- is not satisfied that the death was due to natural causes; or (f) ... require an inquest under any other Act; or (g)
-- the Attorney-General directs; or (h) the Chief Magistrate directs." (2): a coroner "may hold an inquest ... if the
-- coroner considers it desirable"; s 24A: so may the Chief Magistrate. s 26A(2), (3): the senior next of kin may, within
-- 14 days after notice of a decision to hold an inquest under (ea), "in writing, request the coroner not to hold the
-- inquest", and "the coroner, despite section 24(1)(ea), may decline to hold the inquest if he or she is satisfied that
-- it would not be contrary to the public interest or the interests of justice".
DECLARE `Inquest answer` IS ONE OF
    `the coroner has no jurisdiction to investigate this death`
    `the Act no longer applies: the remains are Aboriginal remains`
    `the coroner need not investigate: there is an investigation or inquest in another State or Territory`
    `an inquest must be held`
    `an inquest must be held as a workplace death, but the senior next of kin may ask the coroner not to hold it`
    `the coroner may decline to hold the workplace death inquest`
    `no inquest is required, but one may be held if the coroner or Chief Magistrate considers it desirable`

GIVEN `the coroner considers the death is or may be reportable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the remains have been reported to be Aboriginal remains` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an investigation or inquest in another State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney-General directs an investigation or inquest here` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a Tasmanian connection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner suspects homicide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased was held in care or custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the identity is not known` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased died escaping custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the death occurred during an attempt to detain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another Act requires an inquest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Magistrate directs an inquest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased died at work or from a work accident or injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner is not satisfied the death was natural` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the senior next of kin asked in writing in time not to hold it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner is satisfied not holding it is not contrary to the public interest or justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Inquest answer`
`ss 21-26A -- must there be an inquest` `the coroner considers the death is or may be reportable` `the remains have been reported to be Aboriginal remains` `there is an investigation or inquest in another State or Territory` `the Attorney-General directs an investigation or inquest here` `there is a Tasmanian connection` `the coroner suspects homicide` `the deceased was held in care or custody` `the identity is not known` `the deceased died escaping custody` `the death occurred during an attempt to detain` `another Act requires an inquest` `the Chief Magistrate directs an inquest` `the deceased died at work or from a work accident or injury` `the coroner is not satisfied the death was natural` `the senior next of kin asked in writing in time not to hold it` `the coroner is satisfied not holding it is not contrary to the public interest or justice` MEANS
    IF NOT `the coroner considers the death is or may be reportable`
    THEN `the coroner has no jurisdiction to investigate this death`
    ELSE IF `the remains have been reported to be Aboriginal remains`
         THEN `the Act no longer applies: the remains are Aboriginal remains`
         ELSE IF `there is an investigation or inquest in another State or Territory` AND (NOT `the Attorney-General directs an investigation or inquest here`)
              THEN `the coroner need not investigate: there is an investigation or inquest in another State or Territory`
              ELSE IF `there is a Tasmanian connection` AND `another head`
                   THEN `an inquest must be held`
                   ELSE IF `there is a Tasmanian connection` AND `head (ea)`
                        THEN IF `the senior next of kin asked in writing in time not to hold it` AND `the coroner is satisfied not holding it is not contrary to the public interest or justice`
                             THEN `the coroner may decline to hold the workplace death inquest`
                             ELSE `an inquest must be held as a workplace death, but the senior next of kin may ask the coroner not to hold it`
                        ELSE `no inquest is required, but one may be held if the coroner or Chief Magistrate considers it desirable`
    WHERE
        `another head` MEANS
               `the coroner suspects homicide`
            OR `the deceased was held in care or custody`
            OR `the identity is not known`
            OR `the deceased died escaping custody`
            OR `the death occurred during an attempt to detain`
            OR `another Act requires an inquest`
            OR `the Attorney-General directs an investigation or inquest here`
            OR `the Chief Magistrate directs an inquest`
        `head (ea)` MEANS
            `the deceased died at work or from a work accident or injury` AND `the coroner is not satisfied the death was natural`

§§ `s 25 -- adjournment where a person is charged`

-- s 25(1): if "the coroner is informed, before making a finding, that a person has been charged before justices with
-- any of the offences specified in subsection (2), the coroner -- (a) must, in the absence of reason to the contrary,
-- adjourn the inquest until after the conclusion of the proceedings ...". (2): murder, manslaughter, infanticide or
-- causing grievous bodily harm of the deceased; causing the death by dangerous driving; dangerous driving causing an
-- accident that resulted in the death; an offence under s 32(1) of the Traffic Act 1925 arising out of such an accident;
-- arson in relation to the fire; unlawfully causing the fire or the explosion. (3): after the conclusion, the coroner
-- "may ... resume the adjourned inquest if the coroner is of the opinion that there is sufficient cause". (4): no finding
-- inconsistent with the result if a person was charged on indictment. (5): a resumed inquest proceeds as a fresh one.
-- (7): proceedings are "not taken to be concluded until a further appeal cannot be made ... without an extension of
-- time". (8): a decision not to resume must be reported to the Attorney-General in writing.
DECLARE `Charge` IS ONE OF
    `murder of the deceased`
    `manslaughter of the deceased`
    `infanticide of the deceased`
    `causing grievous bodily harm of the deceased`
    `causing the death by dangerous driving`
    `dangerous driving causing an accident that resulted in the death`
    `a Traffic Act 1925 s 32(1) offence from an accident that resulted in the death`
    `arson in relation to the fire`
    `unlawfully causing the fire`
    `unlawfully causing the explosion`
    `another offence`

DECLARE `Adjournment answer` IS ONE OF
    `section 25 does not require the inquest to be adjourned`
    `the inquest must be adjourned until the criminal proceedings conclude`
    `the coroner may resume the inquest as a fresh inquest`
    `the coroner may not resume the inquest and must tell the Attorney-General`

GIVEN `the charge` IS A `Charge`
      `the person was charged before justices` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner was told before making a finding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is reason to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the criminal proceedings have concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner thinks there is sufficient cause to resume` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Adjournment answer`
`s 25 -- is the inquest adjourned for the criminal case` `the charge` `the person was charged before justices` `the coroner was told before making a finding` `there is reason to the contrary` `the criminal proceedings have concluded` `the coroner thinks there is sufficient cause to resume` MEANS
    IF `the charge` EQUALS `another offence`
       OR (NOT `the person was charged before justices`)
       OR (NOT `the coroner was told before making a finding`)
       OR `there is reason to the contrary`
    THEN `section 25 does not require the inquest to be adjourned`
    ELSE IF NOT `the criminal proceedings have concluded`
         THEN `the inquest must be adjourned until the criminal proceedings conclude`
         ELSE IF `the coroner thinks there is sufficient cause to resume`
              THEN `the coroner may resume the inquest as a fresh inquest`
              ELSE `the coroner may not resume the inquest and must tell the Attorney-General`

§§ `The time limits as regulative rules`

-- "Within 14 days after receiving notice ... may apply" (ss 26(2), 27(3), 44(2)), "may, in writing, request" (s 26A(2)),
-- and "Within 48 hours after receiving notice ... may apply" (ss 37(3), 38(3), 39(4)): the step is a permission, but it
-- is lost when the time passes, so it is modelled as what the person must do to keep it (fork F1 in NOTES.md). The rule
-- starts at the notice and allows the days (or minutes) to the end; FULFILLED means in time, anything else too late.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the person entitled to take the step`
    `the coronial authority`
    `the person who would perform it`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `take the step`
    `provide a copy of the record`
    `perform the autopsy or exhumation`

GIVEN `the time allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the step must be taken within` `the time allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the person entitled to take the step`
    MUST `take the step`
    WITHIN `the time allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person entitled to take the step` BECAUSE "the time for this application or request has passed (ss 26(2), 26A(2), 27(3), 37(3), 38(3), 39(4), 44(2))"

GIVEN `the time of the step` IS A NUMBER, `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `taking the step at` `the time of the step` `satisfies` `the rule` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time of the step`), (EVENT `the person entitled to take the step` `take the step` `the time of the step`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 58C(4): "the coronial authority must provide a copy of the record to the person who made the request within 28
-- days after the request is made or such later period as agreed between the person and the coronial authority."
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the record must be provided within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the coronial authority`
    MUST `provide a copy of the record`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the coronial authority` BECAUSE "the copy was not provided within 28 days or the agreed later period (s 58C(4)); the senior next of kin may appeal (s 58C(10)(b))"

-- s 38(2): "an autopsy must not be performed until 48 hours after the senior next of kin ... has been given notice of
-- the coroner's decision"; s 39(3): "the body must not be exhumed until 48 hours after the request has been made"; s
-- 39(2): "at least 48 hours' notice in writing is given ... before the body is exhumed". A prohibition for a time: the
-- act is barred up to the last minute before 48 hours have passed, and allowed from 48 hours on (fork F2 in NOTES.md),
-- so the rule runs for 2879 minutes.
GIVEN `the minutes barred` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the act is barred for` `the minutes barred` MEANS
    PARTY `the person who would perform it`
    SHANT `perform the autopsy or exhumation`
    WITHIN `the minutes barred`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person who would perform it` BECAUSE "performed before 48 hours had passed (ss 38(2), 39(2), (3))"

-- Whether the act, done at a number of minutes after the start, breaks the 48-hour bar.
GIVEN `the minutes after` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 48-hour bar is broken by acting at` `the minutes after` IF
    `the minutes after` LESS THAN 0
    OR (CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the act is barred for` (`forty-eight hours` MINUS 1)) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the minutes after`), (EVENT `the person who would perform it` `perform the autopsy or exhumation` `the minutes after`))
        WHEN FULFILLED THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE)

§§ `ss 26(2), 26A(2), 27(3), 44(2) -- the 14-day steps`

-- s 26(2): "Within 14 days after receiving notice of a decision under subsection (1) [not to hold an inquest], the
-- senior next of kin ... may apply to the Supreme Court for an order that an inquest be held." s 26A(2): "Within 14 days
-- after receiving notice of a decision under subsection (1) [to hold a workplace death inquest], the senior next of kin
-- ... may, in writing, request the coroner not to hold the inquest." s 27(3): "Within 14 days after receiving notice of
-- the decision not to hold an inquest, the person who requested the inquest may apply to the Supreme Court". s 44(2):
-- the same for a fire or an explosion. "Within 14 days after" a day: the day of notice is not counted, so the last day
-- is the 14th day after it (fork F3 in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `Fourteen-day step` IS ONE OF
    `apply to the Supreme Court for an inquest the coroner or Chief Magistrate decided not to hold`
    `ask the coroner in writing not to hold a workplace death inquest`
    `apply to the Supreme Court for the inquest I asked for and was refused`
    `apply to the Supreme Court for the fire or explosion inquest I asked for and was refused`

DECLARE `Step window` IS ONE OF
    `you may take this step up to and including` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `this step is not open to you`

GIVEN `the step` IS A `Fourteen-day step`, `I am the senior next of kin` IS A BOOLEAN, `I made the request that was refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the step` `is open to me as` `I am the senior next of kin` `or requester` `I made the request that was refused` IF
    CONSIDER `the step`
    WHEN `apply to the Supreme Court for an inquest the coroner or Chief Magistrate decided not to hold` THEN `I am the senior next of kin`
    WHEN `ask the coroner in writing not to hold a workplace death inquest` THEN `I am the senior next of kin`
    OTHERWISE `I made the request that was refused`

-- A grant limited in its own wording: a person outside it is told the step is not open to them.
GIVEN `the step` IS A `Fourteen-day step`
      `I am the senior next of kin` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I made the request that was refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I received notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Step window`
`the 14-day window for` `the step` `I am the senior next of kin` `I made the request that was refused` `the day I received notice` MEANS
    IF `the step` `is open to me as` `I am the senior next of kin` `or requester` `I made the request that was refused`
    THEN `you may take this step up to and including` (`the date` 14 `days after` `the day I received notice`)
    ELSE `this step is not open to you`

-- Whether the step taken on a day is in time. JUST FALSE before the notice or after the 14th day (a period the text
-- fixes); NOTHING for a person the grant does not reach (NOTHING-kind: a grant limited in its own wording).
GIVEN `the step` IS A `Fourteen-day step`
      `I am the senior next of kin` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I made the request that was refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I received notice` IS A DATE
      `the day I take the step` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the 14-day step` `the step` `I am the senior next of kin` `I made the request that was refused` `the day I received notice` `taken on` `the day I take the step` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the step` `is open to me as` `I am the senior next of kin` `or requester` `I made the request that was refused`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the day I take the step` `is before` `the day I received notice`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `taking the step at` (`the days from` `the day I received notice` `to` `the day I take the step`) `satisfies` (`the step must be taken within` 14)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 37(3), 38(3), 39(4) -- the 48-hour applications`

-- s 37(2), (3): if the coroner refuses a request for an autopsy, written reasons; "Within 48 hours after receiving
-- notice of a refusal, the person may apply to the Supreme Court for an order that an autopsy be performed." s 38(1),
-- (3): where the senior next of kin asked the coroner not to direct an autopsy but the coroner decides one is necessary,
-- written notice; "Within 48 hours after receiving notice ..., the senior next of kin ... may apply to the Supreme Court
-- for an order that an autopsy not be performed". s 39(4): "Within 48 hours after receiving notice of the order [to
-- exhume] ..., the senior next of kin ... may apply to the Supreme Court for an order that the body ... not be exhumed".
DECLARE `Forty-eight-hour step` IS ONE OF
    `apply to the Supreme Court for the autopsy I asked for and was refused`
    `apply to the Supreme Court for an order that no autopsy be performed`
    `apply to the Supreme Court for an order that the body not be exhumed`

-- JUST FALSE before the notice or after 48 hours; NOTHING for a person the grant does not reach (NOTHING-kind: a grant
-- limited in its own wording). Times are minutes (tco-dates.l4); exactly 48 hours after the notice is in time.
GIVEN `the step` IS A `Forty-eight-hour step`
      `I am the senior next of kin` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I made the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the moment I received notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the moment I apply` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the 48-hour application` `the step` `I am the senior next of kin` `I made the request` `received at` `the moment I received notice` `made at` `the moment I apply` MEANS
    IF NOT `the step is open to me`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the moment I apply` LESS THAN `the moment I received notice`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `taking the step at` (`the moment I apply` MINUS `the moment I received notice`) `satisfies` (`the step must be taken within` `forty-eight hours`)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the step is open to me` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the step`
            WHEN `apply to the Supreme Court for the autopsy I asked for and was refused` THEN `I made the request`
            WHEN `apply to the Supreme Court for an order that no autopsy be performed` THEN `I am the senior next of kin` AND `I made the request`
            WHEN `apply to the Supreme Court for an order that the body not be exhumed` THEN `I am the senior next of kin`

§§ `ss 38(2), 39 -- the bars on autopsy and exhumation`

-- s 38(2): "Where a request has been made under subsection (1), an autopsy must not be performed until 48 hours after
-- the senior next of kin ... has been given notice of the coroner's decision under that subsection unless the coroner
-- believes that an autopsy needs to be performed immediately." s 38(3): the Supreme Court "may make an order that an
-- autopsy not be performed". Under the 2026-11-05 ruling (d) the bar is encoded: JUST TRUE while it stands, JUST FALSE
-- once it is lifted; where no request was made, or the coroner believes the autopsy is needed at once, s 38 does not
-- bar it (JUST FALSE: a "where" condition fails, and an "unless" met, fork F4).
GIVEN `I asked the coroner not to direct an autopsy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner decided an autopsy is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner believes it must be performed immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Supreme Court has ordered no autopsy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the moment I was given notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the moment of the autopsy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38 -- the autopsy is barred` `I asked the coroner not to direct an autopsy` `the coroner decided an autopsy is necessary` `the coroner believes it must be performed immediately` `the Supreme Court has ordered no autopsy` `the moment I was given notice` `the moment of the autopsy` MEANS
    IF `the Supreme Court has ordered no autopsy`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (NOT `I asked the coroner not to direct an autopsy`) OR (NOT `the coroner decided an autopsy is necessary`) OR `the coroner believes it must be performed immediately`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the 48-hour bar is broken by acting at` (`the moment of the autopsy` MINUS `the moment I was given notice`)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 39(2): "The Chief Magistrate must ensure that at least 48 hours' notice in writing is given to the senior next of
-- kin ... before the body is exhumed unless the Chief Magistrate is satisfied it is not possible to give the notice."
-- (3): "If the senior next of kin ... asks the Chief Magistrate not to exhume the body ..., the body must not be
-- exhumed until 48 hours after the request has been made." (4): the Supreme Court "may make an order that the body not
-- be exhumed". Encoded as the bar (ruling (d)).
GIVEN `notice has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Magistrate is satisfied notice is not possible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the moment notice was given` IS A NUMBER
      `I asked the Chief Magistrate not to exhume` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the moment of my request` IS A NUMBER
      `the Supreme Court has ordered the body not be exhumed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the moment of the exhumation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39 -- the exhumation is barred` `notice has been given` `the Chief Magistrate is satisfied notice is not possible` `the moment notice was given` `I asked the Chief Magistrate not to exhume` `the moment of my request` `the Supreme Court has ordered the body not be exhumed` `the moment of the exhumation` MEANS
    IF `the Supreme Court has ordered the body not be exhumed` OR `barred for want of notice` OR `barred by my request`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `barred for want of notice` MEANS
            IF `the Chief Magistrate is satisfied notice is not possible`
            THEN FALSE
            ELSE IF `notice has been given`
                 THEN `the 48-hour bar is broken by acting at` (`the moment of the exhumation` MINUS `the moment notice was given`)
                 ELSE TRUE
        `barred by my request` MEANS
            `I asked the Chief Magistrate not to exhume`
            AND `the 48-hour bar is broken by acting at` (`the moment of the exhumation` MINUS `the moment of my request`)

§§ `s 32 -- the certificate for disposal of the body`

-- s 32(1): the coroner "must, as soon as reasonably possible, issue a certificate authorising the disposal of human
-- remains." (2): "A certificate ... must not be issued until an application made under section 27 or 37 is disposed of
-- or the time for making such an application has expired." (3): "If the Supreme Court makes an order under section 27
-- or 37, a coroner must not issue a certificate". (4): "Notwithstanding subsection (2), a coroner ... may issue a
-- certificate ... before the time for making an application under section 27 has expired if the person who made a
-- request to hold an inquest ... advises the coroner that he or she does not intend to apply". The bar (ruling (d)):
-- JUST TRUE while barred, JUST FALSE once not.
GIVEN `the Supreme Court has made an order under section 27 or 37` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application under section 27 or 37 is undecided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time for a section 27 application is running` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requester has said they will not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time for a section 37 application is running` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32 -- the disposal certificate is barred` `the Supreme Court has made an order under section 27 or 37` `an application under section 27 or 37 is undecided` `the time for a section 27 application is running` `the requester has said they will not apply` `the time for a section 37 application is running` MEANS
    IF `the Supreme Court has made an order under section 27 or 37`
       OR `an application under section 27 or 37 is undecided`
       OR (`the time for a section 27 application is running` AND (NOT `the requester has said they will not apply`))
       OR `the time for a section 37 application is running`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 52 -- at the inquest`

-- s 52(4): "A person who the coroner considers has a sufficient interest may appear or be represented by an Australian
-- legal practitioner or, with permission of the coroner, by any other person at an inquest, call and examine or
-- cross-examine witnesses, and make submissions, at an inquest." (2): such a person "may make submissions to a coroner
-- at any stage of an investigation". (1): the coroner "may make available any statements or affidavits". A grant
-- limited in its own wording: outside it, NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: a grant limited in its own wording).
DECLARE `Way of appearing` IS ONE OF
    `in person`
    `by an Australian legal practitioner`
    `by another person, with the coroner's permission`
    `by another person, without the coroner's permission`

GIVEN `the coroner considers I have a sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN, `how I appear` IS A `Way of appearing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(4) -- I may appear, examine witnesses and make submissions` `the coroner considers I have a sufficient interest` `how I appear` MEANS
    IF `the coroner considers I have a sufficient interest`
       AND (NOT (`how I appear` EQUALS `by another person, without the coroner's permission`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 29(2), 46(2), 54, 64 -- what can be used in court`

-- s 29(2) and s 46(2): "A record is not evidence in any court of any fact asserted in it." s 54: "A statement or
-- disclosure made by any witness in the course of giving evidence before a coroner at an inquest is not admissible in
-- evidence against that witness in any civil or criminal proceeding in any court other than a prosecution for perjury
-- in the giving of that evidence." s 64: "A coroner is not a compellable witness before a court or tribunal, or in any
-- judicial or other proceedings, in respect of anything that came to the coroner's knowledge in exercising and
-- performing his or her powers and functions under this Act." Flat negatives: JUST FALSE. A perjury prosecution, or use
-- against someone other than the witness, is outside s 54's words: NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: the text is silent; fork F5).
DECLARE `Evidence item` IS ONE OF
    `the coroner's record of a death investigation, as proof of the facts in it`
    `the coroner's record of a fire or explosion investigation, as proof of the facts in it`
    `what a witness said giving evidence at the inquest, against that witness`
    `what a witness said giving evidence at the inquest, against someone else`
    `making the coroner give evidence of what the coroner learned in the investigation`

DECLARE `Proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `a civil proceeding`
    `a criminal proceeding other than for perjury`
    `a prosecution of the witness for perjury in giving that evidence`

GIVEN `the item` IS A `Evidence item`, `the proceeding` IS A `Proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 29, 46, 54, 64 -- it can be used in my court case` `the item` `the proceeding` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `what a witness said giving evidence at the inquest, against that witness` THEN
        IF `the proceeding` EQUALS `a prosecution of the witness for perjury in giving that evidence`
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `what a witness said giving evidence at the inquest, against someone else` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 58C -- copies of the coronial records`

-- s 58C(1): "coronial record means any of the following records in relation to an investigation of a death under this
-- Act: (a) the following records, if held by the Magistrates Court (Coronial Division): (i) a report ... prepared by, or
-- on behalf of, the State Forensic Pathologist or by a pathologist, or medical practitioner, approved under section 35;
-- (ii) any other record or document, including any photograph, that -- (a) contains evidentiary material from the
-- investigation; or (b) is made under this Act in relation to the investigation or death; or (c) is made as part of an
-- autopsy ...; (iii) a transcript, or recording, of oral evidence ...; (b) a record referred to in paragraph (a) if the
-- record is able to be provided lawfully to the Magistrates Court (Coronial Division) under this Act or any other Act."
-- (2), (3): the senior next of kin "may request", "in writing to a coronial authority" (the Chief Magistrate or the
-- coroner with jurisdiction). (4): "the coronial authority must provide a copy ... within 28 days after the request is
-- made or such later period as agreed". (5): it "may only refuse ... if ... satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that" one
-- of four grounds holds; (6): it may then redact or modify a copy. (10)-(12): appeals.
DECLARE `Kind of record` IS ONE OF
    `a pathology or autopsy report by the State Forensic Pathologist or an approved pathologist or practitioner`
    `a record or photograph containing evidentiary material, made under the Act, or made in the autopsy`
    `a transcript or recording of oral evidence`
    `some other document`

DECLARE `Refusal ground` IS ONE OF
    `no ground for refusal`
    `release is prevented by section 57 or another law`
    `an unreasonable intrusion on another person's privacy, contrary to the public interest`
    `likely to prejudice an investigation, law enforcement or a fair trial`
    `contrary to national security or personal security`

DECLARE `Records answer` IS ONE OF
    `you must be given a copy by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the authority may refuse, or give you a redacted or modified copy`
    `this is not a coronial record`
    `this is not a request section 58C covers`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of record`, `it is held by or lawfully obtainable by the Coronial Division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a record of kind` `the kind` `held` `it is held by or lawfully obtainable by the Coronial Division` `is a coronial record` IF
    `it is held by or lawfully obtainable by the Coronial Division` AND (NOT (`the kind` EQUALS `some other document`))

-- The last day: 28 days after the request, or a later agreed day if one was agreed.
GIVEN `the day of the request` IS A DATE, `a later period was agreed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the agreed last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the s 58C(4) last day for` `the day of the request` `agreed` `a later period was agreed` `the agreed last day` MEANS
    IF `a later period was agreed`
    THEN `the later of` (`the date` 28 `days after` `the day of the request`) `and` `the agreed last day`
    ELSE `the date` 28 `days after` `the day of the request`

GIVEN `I am the senior next of kin` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I asked in writing to the Chief Magistrate or the coroner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind` IS A `Kind of record`
      `it is held by or lawfully obtainable by the Coronial Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground the authority is satisfied of` IS A `Refusal ground`
      `the day of the request` IS A DATE
      `a later period was agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreed last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Records answer`
`s 58C -- must I be given a copy of the record` `I am the senior next of kin` `I asked in writing to the Chief Magistrate or the coroner` `the kind` `it is held by or lawfully obtainable by the Coronial Division` `the ground the authority is satisfied of` `the day of the request` `a later period was agreed` `the agreed last day` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I am the senior next of kin`) OR (NOT `I asked in writing to the Chief Magistrate or the coroner`)
    THEN `this is not a request section 58C covers`
    ELSE IF NOT (`a record of kind` `the kind` `held` `it is held by or lawfully obtainable by the Coronial Division` `is a coronial record`)
         THEN `this is not a coronial record`
         ELSE IF `the ground the authority is satisfied of` EQUALS `no ground for refusal`
              THEN `you must be given a copy by` (`the s 58C(4) last day for` `the day of the request` `agreed` `a later period was agreed` `the agreed last day`)
              ELSE `the authority may refuse, or give you a redacted or modified copy`

-- s 58C(10)(b): the senior next of kin may appeal "a failure to provide a copy of the coronial record as required under
-- subsection (4)". The duty is run as a trace to the day asked about: BREACH (not provided, or provided late) is a
-- failure, JUST TRUE; provided in time, or the time not yet over, JUST FALSE (fork F6).
GIVEN `the day of the request` IS A DATE
      `a later period was agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreed last day` IS A DATE
      `the copy has been provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was provided` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 58C(4), (10)(b) -- the authority has failed to provide the copy` `the day of the request` `a later period was agreed` `the agreed last day` `the copy has been provided` `the day it was provided` `the day asked about` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the record must be provided within` (`the days from` `the day of the request` `to` (`the s 58C(4) last day for` `the day of the request` `agreed` `a later period was agreed` `the agreed last day`))) 0 `the events`
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE IF `the trace is still waiting` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the day provided, counted` MEANS `the days from` `the day of the request` `to` `the day it was provided`
        `the day asked, counted` MEANS `the days from` `the day of the request` `to` `the day asked about`
        `the deadline, counted` MEANS `the days from` `the day of the request` `to` (`the s 58C(4) last day for` `the day of the request` `agreed` `a later period was agreed` `the agreed last day`)
        `provided by the day asked about` MEANS `the copy has been provided` AND (`the day provided, counted` AT MOST `the day asked, counted`)
        `the events` MEANS
            IF `provided by the day asked about`
            THEN LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day provided, counted`), (EVENT `the coronial authority` `provide a copy of the record` `the day provided, counted`)
            ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day asked, counted`)
        `the trace is still waiting` MEANS
            (NOT `provided by the day asked about`) AND (`the day asked, counted` AT MOST `the deadline, counted`)

-- s 58C(11): "An appeal under subsection (10) is to be determined by -- (a) if the appeal relates to a request ...
-- determined by the Chief Magistrate as a coronial authority -- the Supreme Court; and (b) in any other case -- the
-- Chief Magistrate." (12): a further appeal from the Chief Magistrate lies to the Supreme Court.
DECLARE `Appeal forum` IS ONE OF
    `the Supreme Court`
    `the Chief Magistrate, with a further appeal to the Supreme Court`

GIVEN `the Chief Magistrate determined my request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Appeal forum`
`s 58C(11) -- who hears my records appeal` `the Chief Magistrate determined my request` MEANS
    IF `the Chief Magistrate determined my request`
    THEN `the Supreme Court`
    ELSE `the Chief Magistrate, with a further appeal to the Supreme Court`

§§ `ss 58, 58A -- reopening and voiding findings`

-- s 58(1): "The Chief Magistrate may reopen an investigation and re-examine some or all of its findings, or direct
-- another coroner to do so, if the Chief Magistrate is satisfied that -- (a) the investigation was or may have been
-- tainted by fraud; or (b) ... not sufficiently thorough or was compromised by evidentiary or procedural irregularity;
-- or (c) there are mistakes in the record of the findings; or (d) new facts or evidence affecting the findings have come
-- to light; or (e) the findings were not supported by the evidence; or (f) there is another compelling reason". (2):
-- on the Chief Magistrate's own initiative, or "(b) the application of a person who the Chief Magistrate considers has a
-- sufficient interest in the findings". (3): "However, the Chief Magistrate is not to exercise power under subsection
-- (1) if an application under section 58A ... (a) is before the Supreme Court; or (b) has been rejected by the Supreme
-- Court and the Chief Magistrate's reasons ... would be the same or substantially the same as the grounds of that
-- application." (7): "A person may appeal to the Supreme Court if the Chief Magistrate refuses an application made by
-- the person under subsection (2)(b)". s 58A(1), (3): "Any person may apply to the Supreme Court for an order that all
-- or any of the findings of an inquest are void", which the Court may make if satisfied of the same six grounds; (4):
-- it is then to order the Chief Magistrate to reopen the inquest or hold a new one, or direct another coroner to.
DECLARE `Ground for reopening` IS ONE OF
    `fraud`
    `not sufficiently thorough, or evidentiary or procedural irregularity`
    `mistakes in the record of the findings`
    `new facts or evidence affecting the findings`
    `findings not supported by the evidence`
    `another compelling reason`
    `no such ground`

DECLARE `Reopening answer` IS ONE OF
    `the Chief Magistrate may reopen the investigation on your application`
    `the Chief Magistrate may not reopen it while a section 58A application is before the Supreme Court`
    `the Chief Magistrate may not reopen it on substantially the grounds the Supreme Court rejected`
    `the Chief Magistrate may not reopen it without being satisfied of a ground; a refusal of your application can be appealed`
    `you cannot apply, though the Chief Magistrate may reopen it on his or her own initiative`

GIVEN `the Chief Magistrate considers I have a sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a section 58A application is before the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a section 58A application was rejected on substantially the same grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground the Chief Magistrate is satisfied of` IS A `Ground for reopening`
GIVETH A `Reopening answer`
`s 58 -- can the investigation be reopened on my application` `the Chief Magistrate considers I have a sufficient interest` `a section 58A application is before the Supreme Court` `a section 58A application was rejected on substantially the same grounds` `the ground the Chief Magistrate is satisfied of` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Chief Magistrate considers I have a sufficient interest`
    THEN `you cannot apply, though the Chief Magistrate may reopen it on his or her own initiative`
    ELSE IF `a section 58A application is before the Supreme Court`
         THEN `the Chief Magistrate may not reopen it while a section 58A application is before the Supreme Court`
         ELSE IF `a section 58A application was rejected on substantially the same grounds`
              THEN `the Chief Magistrate may not reopen it on substantially the grounds the Supreme Court rejected`
              ELSE IF `the ground the Chief Magistrate is satisfied of` EQUALS `no such ground`
                   THEN `the Chief Magistrate may not reopen it without being satisfied of a ground; a refusal of your application can be appealed`
                   ELSE `the Chief Magistrate may reopen the investigation on your application`

-- s 58A: only the findings "of an inquest" (NOTHING-kind: a grant limited in its own wording, for an investigation with
-- no inquest); "if the court is satisfied" of a ground (JUST FALSE when none).
GIVEN `there was an inquest` IS A BOOLEAN, `the ground the Supreme Court is satisfied of` IS A `Ground for reopening`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 58A -- the Supreme Court may declare the inquest findings void` `there was an inquest` `the ground the Supreme Court is satisfied of` MEANS
    IF NOT `there was an inquest`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the ground the Supreme Court is satisfied of` EQUALS `no such ground`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 59A(4), 60-63 -- property held for the investigation`

-- s 60(1): "This section applies to a person claiming ownership of, a lien over, or some other present or future right
-- to possession of, an article, substance or thing that is in the legal custody of a coroner for the purposes of an
-- investigation." (2): the coroner "may, on application by the Director of Public Prosecutions or a person to whom this
-- section applies, make such orders as the coroner thinks fit as to the care and control of the article ... pending the
-- conclusion of the investigation." (3): each "entitled to be heard". s 61(1): "On the conclusion of an investigation or
-- on the adjournment or conclusion of an inquest, a coroner must make such orders as the coroner thinks fit for the
-- custody, care and control, or the disposition, of each article ... unless the coroner is satisfied that [it] will be,
-- or is likely to be, required for the purpose of other legal proceedings." (2): entitled to be heard. s 62(1): "Where
-- there is a substantial change in the circumstances ..., the coroner who made the order may, on the application of ...
-- a person to whom section 60 applies, vary or revoke that order". s 63: such a person "may apply to the Supreme Court
-- for a review of an order made by a coroner under section 60, 61 or 62."
DECLARE `Stage of the investigation` IS ONE OF
    `the investigation is continuing`
    `the investigation has concluded, or the inquest is adjourned or concluded, and no order has yet been made`
    `the coroner has made an order about the item`

DECLARE `Property answer` IS ONE OF
    `section 60 does not apply to you`
    `you may apply to the coroner for orders about its care and control, and are entitled to be heard`
    `the coroner must make orders for its custody or disposition, and you are entitled to be heard`
    `the coroner need not make orders now: it is likely to be needed for other legal proceedings`
    `you may ask the Supreme Court to review the order, or the coroner to vary or revoke it`
    `you may ask the Supreme Court to review the order`

GIVEN `I claim ownership, a lien or a right to possess the item` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item is in the coroner's legal custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stage` IS A `Stage of the investigation`
      `the coroner is satisfied it is likely to be needed for other proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been a substantial change in circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Property answer`
`ss 60-63 -- what I can do about my property held by the coroner` `I claim ownership, a lien or a right to possess the item` `the item is in the coroner's legal custody` `the stage` `the coroner is satisfied it is likely to be needed for other proceedings` `there has been a substantial change in circumstances` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I claim ownership, a lien or a right to possess the item`) OR (NOT `the item is in the coroner's legal custody`)
    THEN `section 60 does not apply to you`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the stage`
         WHEN `the investigation is continuing` THEN `you may apply to the coroner for orders about its care and control, and are entitled to be heard`
         WHEN `the investigation has concluded, or the inquest is adjourned or concluded, and no order has yet been made` THEN
             IF `the coroner is satisfied it is likely to be needed for other proceedings`
             THEN `the coroner need not make orders now: it is likely to be needed for other legal proceedings`
             ELSE `the coroner must make orders for its custody or disposition, and you are entitled to be heard`
         WHEN `the coroner has made an order about the item` THEN
             IF `there has been a substantial change in circumstances`
             THEN `you may ask the Supreme Court to review the order, or the coroner to vary or revoke it`
             ELSE `you may ask the Supreme Court to review the order`

-- s 59A(4): where a police officer took a thing in an emergency and no coroner was then investigating: "(a) the police
-- officer may retain [it] pending the commencement of an investigation; (b) if an investigation is commenced within 12
-- months of the power being exercised -- ... on the giving of the notice the article ... is in the legal custody, care
-- and control of the coroner; (c) if an investigation is not commenced within 12 months ..., the article ... is to be --
-- (i) returned to the person from whom it was taken or, if that person is not legally entitled to take possession of
-- it, to the person who is so entitled; or (ii) disposed of as the Commissioner of Police directs if it is illicit."
-- s 59A(3)(c): where a coroner was investigating, on notice it is in the coroner's custody. "Within 12 months of" a day:
-- an investigation commenced on the anniversary is in time (fork F7).
DECLARE `Seized item answer` IS ONE OF
    `it is in the coroner's custody: section 60 applies to it`
    `the police may keep it until an investigation begins or 12 months pass`
    `it must be returned to the person it was taken from, or to the person entitled to it`
    `it is to be disposed of as the Commissioner of Police directs`

GIVEN `a coroner was investigating when it was taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was taken` IS A DATE
      `an investigation has commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the investigation commenced` IS A DATE
      `the item is illicit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Seized item answer`
`s 59A -- what happens to the item the police took` `a coroner was investigating when it was taken` `the day it was taken` `an investigation has commenced` `the day the investigation commenced` `the item is illicit` `the day asked about` MEANS
    IF `a coroner was investigating when it was taken`
       OR (`an investigation has commenced`
           AND (NOT (`the day the investigation commenced` `is after` `the end of 12 months`))
           AND (NOT (`the day the investigation commenced` `is after` `the day asked about`)))
    THEN `it is in the coroner's custody: section 60 applies to it`
    ELSE IF NOT (`the day asked about` `is after` `the end of 12 months`)
         THEN `the police may keep it until an investigation begins or 12 months pass`
         ELSE IF `the item is illicit`
              THEN `it is to be disposed of as the Commissioner of Police directs`
              ELSE `it must be returned to the person it was taken from, or to the person entitled to it`
    WHERE
        `the end of 12 months` MEANS `the anniversary` 1 `years after` `the day it was taken`

§§ `Penalties`

-- The offences a person may commit, with the maximum fine (penalty units) and imprisonment (months). The value of a
-- penalty unit is set by the Penalty Units and Other Penalties Act 1987, which is not deposited: the answer stays in
-- penalty units.
DECLARE `Offence` IS ONE OF
    `not reporting a reportable death (s 19)`
    `not giving the coroner information after reporting a death (s 20(1))`
    `entering or interfering with a restricted death scene (s 34(3))`
    `not giving the coroner information after asking for a fire investigation (s 42(3))`
    `entering or interfering with a restricted fire or explosion scene (s 49(3))`
    `disobeying a coroner's summons, order or direction without reasonable excuse (s 53(4))`
    `publishing a report contrary to a coroner's order (s 57(2))`
    `publishing a released coronial record contrary to an order (s 58C(9))`
    `hindering or obstructing a coroner (s 65)`
    `insulting a coroner, interrupting an inquest or causing a disturbance (s 66)`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Offence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most penalty units for` `the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `publishing a report contrary to a coroner's order (s 57(2))` THEN 50
    WHEN `publishing a released coronial record contrary to an order (s 58C(9))` THEN 50
    WHEN `insulting a coroner, interrupting an inquest or causing a disturbance (s 66)` THEN 50
    WHEN `hindering or obstructing a coroner (s 65)` THEN 20
    OTHERWISE 10

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Offence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most months of imprisonment for` `the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `entering or interfering with a restricted death scene (s 34(3))` THEN 3
    WHEN `entering or interfering with a restricted fire or explosion scene (s 49(3))` THEN 3
    WHEN `disobeying a coroner's summons, order or direction without reasonable excuse (s 53(4))` THEN 3
    WHEN `hindering or obstructing a coroner (s 65)` THEN 6
    WHEN `insulting a coroner, interrupting an inquest or causing a disturbance (s 66)` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 0
